
<html>
<title>Settings</title>
<body>
<h1>Settings</h1>
<p>
<IMG SRC="images/menu_settings.png" border="0" width="400" height ="236">
</p>
<h2>Wav file and Real Cassette Settings</h2>
<p>
Open window to change settings for wav files and <a href="ComputerRealCassette.htm">Real Cassette Support</a>.
</p>
<h2>Equalization</h2>
<p>
Select one of the sub menu items to adjust sound equalization. Default 'TV Speaker' is selected. For other sound information see the <a href="ComputerSound.htm">Sound</a> section.
</p>
<h2>Window</h2>
<p>
Sub menu items for Emma 02 <a href="MainWindow.htm">Window</a> handling.
</p>
<h2>CPU Type</h2>
<p>
<IMG SRC="images/menu_cpu.png" border="0" width="506" height ="236">
</p>
<p>
Select one of the sub menu items (highlighted in yellow) to choose the CPU type used for all emulated computers. Default CDP1805 is selected allowing a more extensive instruction set than the CDP1802. The CDP1805 is backward compatible with the CDP1802 which was used in most emulated computers. 
</p>
<p>
<B>Note:</B> The <a href="https://www.emma02.hobby-site.com/fred1.html">FRED 1</a> will always be emulated using a <a href="https://www.emma02.hobby-site.com/system00.html">SYSTEM00</a> and the <a href="https://www.emma02.hobby-site.com/microtutor.html">Microtutor</a>, <a href="https://www.emma02.hobby-site.com/coin_arcade.html">RCA Video Coin Arcade</a> and <a href="https://www.emma02.hobby-site.com/fred1_5.html">FRED 1.5</a> will always be emulated using a <a href="https://www.emma02.hobby-site.com/1801.html">CDP1801</a>. This is due to the fact that these CPUs were used in the real machines and they are not fully compatible with the <a href="https://www.emma02.hobby-site.com/1802.html">CDP1802</a>.
</p>
<h2>Startup Values</h2>
<p>
<IMG SRC="images/menu_startup.png" border="0" width="522" height ="236">
</p>
<p>
Select one of the sub menu items (highlighted in yellow) to set the startup values for CPU registers, RAM or Video RAM. The following options can be chosen:
</p>
<UL>
<LI>
Zero: CPU registers, RAM content or Video RAM content is set to 0 on startup
<LI>
Random: CPU registers, RAM content or Video RAM content is set to a random value on startup 
<LI>
Dynamic: RAM content or Video RAM content is set similar to the COMX Dynamic RAM content on startup. This content is a repeating pattern of 64 values 255 (FF) followed by 64 values of 0, one random location of these 128 values will have a random value instead of 0 or 255.
</UL>
<h2>Function and Hot Keys</h2>
<p>
Open <a href="MainFunctionKeys.htm">Function and Hot Keys</a> window.
</p>
<h2>Use Numeric Keypad</h2>
<p>
Unselect this menu item if your PC does NOT have a numeric keypad (numpad). If unselected all keymap definitions will (where possible) not use any key definitions from the PC numeric keypad.
</p>
<h2>Default keyboard</h2>
<p>
<IMG SRC="images/menu_keyboard.png" border="0" width="538" height ="324">
</p>
<p>
Default keyboard mapping is defined for a US keyboard layout. However a few different other layouts (Dutch, German, French, Swedish / Finnish) are provided and can be selected via this menu. See section <a href="KeyMappingDefault.htm">Default Keyboard</a> for more details.
</p>
<h2>COMX SuperBoard</h2>
<p>
Only used in the COMX and COMiX emulators if a <a href="ComxSb.htm">COMX SuperBoard</a> is configured. Popup menu will allow for 'Online' , USB and backup settings. 
</p>
<p>
For more information about the Super Board (SB) project please see our <a href="http://www.comx35.com/superboard.html">COMX Super Board</a> page.
</p>
</body>
</html>
